# tools/al/ales_stereo_reverb_console_predelay_witness.rish — the stereo console pre-delay: the dry-composed pre-delay against the dry, across a stereo master (ALES197).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES197.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-103451_fill-ales197-lotus-stereo-console-predelay.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb_predelay.rye (ALES195 — the wet-domain stereo pre-delay whose faults this forwards and whose full-wet edge this
# equals); lotus/stereo_reverb_mix.rye (ALES193 — the per-channel wet/dry blend this reuses and whose no-gap edge this equals);
# lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye (ALES191 — the named-room stereo wet); lotus/clock.rye (ALES5 — the sample clock); lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the
# Clip each channel holds); lotus/pan.rye (ALES — the StereoClip).
#
# lotus/stereo_reverb_console_predelay.rye gives the stereo reverb its classic console pre-delay, heard against the dry — the thin twin ALES196
# named next. It snapshots each channel's DRY span, reverberates the master wet in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset UNCHANGED, forms
# each channel's pre-delayed wet (pw[i] = 0 for i < predelay, else wet[i - predelay]), then blends each sample of each channel out[i] =
# saturate((den-num)·dry[i]/den + num·pw[i]/den) — ALES193's per-channel balance over ALES195's per-channel reindex, run per ear with no
# cross-channel read, saturated once, no new audio arithmetic. The selftest proves: at predelay = 0 the span equals stereo_reverb_mix byte for byte
# on both channels; at mix = 0 each channel the exact dry at any pre-delay; at mix = den it equals stereo_reverb_predelay byte for byte on both; a
# mid pre-delay and mid mix the weighted average per channel of its own dry and its own pre-delayed wet; the image is held, the channels leave
# balanced, silence stays silence; and the faults forward (BadMix, BadPredelay, DurationTooLong, BadRange), both channels untouched. Purely local —
# one StereoClip, four bounded stack snapshots; no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_reverb_console_predelay_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: Language EN — ALES196 finished the console pre-delay for a mono clip (the voice first, then the delayed room blooming behind it); a keeper mixing a stereo master still had only the wet-domain stereo pre-delay. This rung is the thin twin ALES196 named next: the same dry-composed blend, over both channels of a StereoClip, one shared gap, the image held — and with it the pre-delay axis stands whole for mono and stereo."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: Style Radiant — the three edges are stated positively and proven exact on both ears: at predelay = 0 the span equals stereo_reverb_mix byte for byte (no gap is exactly the stereo wet/dry mix), at mix = 0 each channel is the exact dry at any pre-delay (the room fully closed is the identity), and at mix = den it equals stereo_reverb_predelay byte for byte (fully open is exactly the wet-domain stereo pre-delay). The pre-delay is a named duration in milliseconds and the mix a named fraction, so both mean the same at any rate."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: Lens TAME — one StereoClip of i16 PCM, a validated clock, ALES191's fixed banks, and four bounded stack snapshots (two dry, two wet, max_clip = 4096 samples each); NO new audio arithmetic — ALES193's per-channel blend summed in i64 and saturated once so it can never wrap, over ALES195's per-channel bounded reindex with a true-zero gap, no cross-channel read; StereoReverbConsolePredelayError = stereo_reverb_predelay.StereoReverbPredelayError || BadMix, DurationTooLong / BadRange / BadPredelay / BadMix by name before any write, the dry snapshots reads only so a refusal leaves both channels untouched and balanced; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_console_predelay"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_console_predelay.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_console_predelay.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay line"

# This rung composes ALES195's stereo pre-delay and ALES193's stereo mix over their public APIs — re-prove both still stand green beside it.
let predelay = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_predelay.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_predelay && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_predelay selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-predelay' && echo yes"]
assert (trim predelay.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: the ALES195 wet-domain stereo pre-delay regressed under its console composition"

let mix = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_mix.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_mix && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_mix selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-mix' && echo yes"]
assert (trim mix.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: the ALES193 stereo wet/dry mix regressed under its console composition"

say "ales-stereo-reverb-console-predelay: GREEN — the stereo console pre-delay: the dry-composed pre-delay heard against the dry, now across a stereo master. Snapshot each channel's dry span, reverberate the master wet in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, form each channel's pre-delayed wet (pw[i] = 0 for i < predelay, else wet[i - predelay]), then blend each channel out[i] = saturate((den-num)·dry[i]/den + num·pw[i]/den) — ALES193's per-channel balance over ALES195's per-channel reindex, run per ear with no cross-channel read, saturated once, no new audio arithmetic. Proven: at predelay = 0 exactly stereo_reverb_mix byte for byte on both channels; at mix = 0 each channel the exact dry at any pre-delay; at mix = den exactly stereo_reverb_predelay byte for byte on both; a mid pre-delay and mid mix the weighted average per channel; the image is held, the channels leave balanced, silence stays silence; a bad fraction refuses BadMix, a pre-delay past the span BadPredelay, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving both channels untouched; the ALES195 stereo pre-delay and ALES193 stereo mix stay GREEN beside it. The pre-delay axis now stands whole for mono and stereo — the reverb's which/how-much/when complete on both; a damping knob (a high-frequency roll-off inside the tail) is the next genuinely new primitive."
